  "preamble": "Fortition of the palatal glide [j] to a palatalized voiced stop [dʲ]. In Samoyedic, Proto-Samoyedic word-initial *j is kept in Nenets and Enets, becomes /tʲ/ in Selkup, and /dʲ/ in the other branches; Nganasan shows it in native words (*jïntə 'bow' > динтə djintə) and in early Turkic loans (*jür 'hundred' > дир djir).",
  "phoneticEffects": "Fortition, Occlusion",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Nganasan",
      "languageFamily": "Samoyedic",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Proto-Samoyedic *jïntə 'bow' (< Proto-Uralic *joŋse)",
          "to": "динтə (djintə) 'bow'",
          "note": "Initial *j- is kept, as a palatalized stop, only in Nganasan; it is lost in the other branches."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Samoyedic *jür 'hundred' (< Proto-Turkic *yǖŕ)",
          "to": "дир (djir) 'hundred'",
          "note": "Compare Tundra Nenets юрˮ (yur), which keeps the glide."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
